/// Customers contains customer information used to analyze sales and business activity by customer. The table represents customer dimension records and supports Slowly Changing Dimension Type 2 (SCD Type 2) history. Customer Key is the surrogate key used to identify a specific version of a customer record and is used for relationships with the Sales table. Customer ID is the business identifier originating from the source system and identifies the customer independently of historical versions. The table contains customer company, contact, address, geographic, and communication information. Effective From and Effective To define the validity period of each customer record version. Is Current identifies whether a record represents the current version of the customer. Historical records should not be treated as duplicate customers; they represent different versions of the same business customer over time. Use Customer ID for business-level customer identification and Customer Key only for relationships and technical modeling.
table Customers
	lineageTag: 8eecd2cd-01ee-4874-bd56-5dbe45669ea6
	sourceLineageTag: [gold].[dim_customer]

	/// Surrogate key that uniquely identifies a specific version of a customer record in the Customers dimension. It is a technical key used for relationships with Sales and should not be treated as the customer's business identifier.
	column CustomerKey
		dataType: int64
		formatString: 0
		lineageTag: 65612bf9-d321-429d-a18d-59ce02ddbf04
		sourceLineageTag: CustomerKey
		summarizeBy: none
		sourceColumn: CustomerKey

		changedProperty = Description

		annotation SummarizationSetBy = Automatic

	/// Business identifier of the customer from the source system. The same Customer ID can appear in multiple dimension records when customer attributes change over time because this dimension uses Slowly Changing Dimension Type 2.
	column CustomerID
		dataType: string
		lineageTag: 217dbfa4-0d31-418f-abd5-b246b8463a88
		sourceLineageTag: CustomerID
